<article class="article-wrap">
  <div class="article-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="article-tag">E-Commerce · Catalog Guide</div>
      <h1>How to Share WhatsApp Catalog & Product Links to Boost Sales</h1>
      <div class="article-meta">
        <span>Published September 2026</span><span>·</span><span>6 min read</span><span>·</span><span>Author: LinkWA Commerce Team</span>
      </div>
      <p class="article-intro">Instead of losing customers to sluggish websites and abandoned checkout carts, modern businesses are selling directly through WhatsApp Catalogs. Here is how to create, share, and promote your WhatsApp catalog and product links to close more sales with less friction.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">

      <div class="callout">
        <strong>🛍️ In a Nutshell:</strong> WhatsApp Business lets you share a link to your <strong>entire storefront</strong> or to a <strong>single specific product</strong>. Combine catalog links with a <a href="/">LinkWA custom QR code</a> or pre-filled click-to-chat link to let shoppers buy with a single tap.
      </div>

      <h2>What is a WhatsApp Catalog Link?</h2>
      <p>A WhatsApp Catalog link is a dedicated URL that opens your mobile storefront directly inside the WhatsApp app. Customers can:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Browse high-resolution product photos and price tags</li>
        <li>Read product descriptions and SKU details</li>
        <li>Add multiple products to an in-app shopping cart</li>
        <li>Send the cart directly to your sales team with one tap to confirm payment and delivery</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The standard WhatsApp catalog link format looks like:</p>
      <pre><code>https://wa.me/c/[country code][phone number]</code></pre>
      <p>Notice the <code>/c/</code> in the URL structure — this indicates a catalog storefront rather than a standard one-on-one text window.</p>

      <h2>How to Find and Copy Your Entire Catalog Link (Step-by-Step)</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open the <strong>WhatsApp Business app</strong> on your phone.</li>
        <li>On Android, tap <strong>More options (⋮)</strong> → <strong>Business tools</strong> → <strong>Catalog</strong>. On iPhone, tap the <strong>Settings / Tools</strong> tab → <strong>Catalog</strong>.</li>
        <li>Tap the <strong>Share icon (or three dots)</strong> in the top-right corner.</li>
        <li>Select <strong>Share link</strong> or <strong>Copy link</strong>.</li>
        <li>Your catalog URL is now copied to your clipboard.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>How to Share an Individual Product Item Link</h2>
      <p>Want to promote a single trending dress, electronic gadget, or consultation package on Instagram Stories or email? Share the direct item link:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Inside <strong>Business tools → Catalog</strong>, tap the specific item you want to share.</li>
        <li>Tap the <strong>Link / Share icon</strong> at the top right of the product detail card.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>Copy link</strong>.</li>
        <li>Share this unique item URL. When clicked, it opens that exact product card with a prominent <em>"Message Business about this item"</em> button.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>5 High-Converting Ways to Distribute Your Catalog Links</h2>

      <h3>1. Turn Your Catalog Link into an In-Store QR Code</h3>
      <p>Offline retail and restaurants can convert physical foot traffic into repeat digital buyers. Paste your catalog link into <a href="/">LinkWA's QR code generator</a> to produce high-resolution, branded QR codes. Display them on:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Storefront windows for after-hours window shopping</li>
        <li>Restaurant dining tables for real-time digital ordering (learn more in our <a href="/blog/whatsapp-qr-code-restaurant-menu">restaurant menu QR guide</a>)</li>
        <li>Product packaging for easy 1-tap re-ordering (see our <a href="/blog/whatsapp-qr-code-product-packaging">packaging QR code guide</a>)</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>2. Add Your Catalog to Your Instagram Bio & Stories</h3>
      <p>Instagram is prime real estate for D2C brands. Place your catalog link directly in your Instagram bio or use the native "Link Sticker" in Instagram Stories alongside product teasers: <em>"Tap to view pricing & full specifications on our WhatsApp Catalog."</em></p>

      <h3>3. Embed "Buy on WhatsApp" Buttons on Your Website</h3>
      <p>If you run a WordPress, Shopify, or static website, you don't need complicated payment gateway setups. Add a "Buy on WhatsApp" button linking directly to the product's catalog link or to a pre-filled <a href="/blog/how-to-create-whatsapp-link">wa.me link</a> like:</p>
      <pre><code>https://wa.me/919876543210?text=Hi!%20I%20want%20to%20order%20the%20Leather%20Handbag</code></pre>

      <h3>4. Use Catalog Links in Click-to-WhatsApp Facebook & Instagram Ads</h3>
      <p>Run Meta ads that skip traditional landing pages entirely. When users tap your ad, they land directly inside your WhatsApp catalog where conversion rates are often <strong>2x to 4x higher</strong> than standard mobile landing pages. Read our tutorial on <a href="/blog/whatsapp-link-facebook-ads-lead-generation">WhatsApp Facebook Ads lead generation</a>.</p>

      <h3>5. Send Automated Catalog Links in Welcome Messages</h3>
      <p>When a new customer messages your business number, greet them with an instant automated response containing your catalog link: <em>"Welcome to [Store Name]! Check out our current collection and prices here: [Catalog Link]."</em> Explore our library of <a href="/blog/whatsapp-business-auto-reply-message-samples">35+ WhatsApp Business auto-reply templates</a>.</p>

      <h2>Catalog Link vs. Pre-Filled wa.me Link: Which is Better?</h2>
      <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1.5rem 0; font-size: 14px;">
        <thead>
          <tr style="background: var(--surf); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--bd); text-align: left;">
            <th style="padding: 10px;">Feature</th>
            <th style="padding: 10px;">WhatsApp Catalog Link (wa.me/c/...)</th>
            <th style="padding: 10px;">Pre-Filled Link (wa.me/.../?text=)</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bd);">
            <td style="padding: 10px; font-weight: 600;">Best Used For</td>
            <td style="padding: 10px;">Multi-item browsing, visual shopping, menus</td>
            <td style="padding: 10px;">Single service booking, urgent quotes, fast chat</td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bd);">
            <td style="padding: 10px; font-weight: 600;">Visual Experience</td>
            <td style="padding: 10px;">Full product gallery with photos & prices</td>
            <td style="padding: 10px;">Direct text chat window with pre-typed text</td>
          </tr>
          <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bd);">
            <td style="padding: 10px; font-weight: 600;">App Requirement</td>
            <td style="padding: 10px;">Requires WhatsApp Business App</td>
            <td style="padding: 10px;">Works on standard WhatsApp & Business</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <h3>Why is my WhatsApp catalog link showing 'Catalog not available'?</h3>
      <p>Ensure your WhatsApp Business account is active, your catalog is set to visible, and your products have been approved by Meta's commerce review. Items violating WhatsApp's Commerce Policy (such as supplements, weapons, or adult products) will be rejected.</p>

      <h3>Can customers buy and pay directly inside the WhatsApp catalog?</h3>
      <p>In select countries (like India, Brazil, and Singapore), WhatsApp offers native in-chat UPI and credit card payments. In other countries, customers send you their cart, and you can provide payment links (Stripe, Razorpay, PayPal) or Cash on Delivery instructions directly in the chat.</p>

      <h3>Can I hide out-of-stock items in my WhatsApp catalog?</h3>
      <p>Yes. In WhatsApp Business, edit any product and toggle off the <em>"Item in stock"</em> switch. The item will be immediately hidden from customer view without deleting your description.</p>

